{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/815142-nwod-ghosts-in-the-hedge","id":815142,"title":"(nWoD) Ghosts in the hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T17:55:39-08:00","id":815142,"title":"(nWoD) Ghosts in the hedge","content":"I have always been led to believe a incorporeal non-Fae being in the hedge became corporeal.<br /> <br /> But I cannot reference to anything like this in any books.<br /> <br /> Have I been told incorrectly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:12:06-08:00","id":815157,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for ghosts in particular then you won't find the reference, ostensibly because ghosts in 1e had a lower degree of mobility than could reasonably be expected to let them in, but Equinox Road's crossover section notes on p73 that if a pack's totem spirit accompanies them into the Hedge it's immediately Materialized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T03:23:56-08:00","id":815339,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I also remember someone in this forum saying that spirits who 'go native' to the Hedge effectually become hobgoblins, gaining a corporeal body and swapping their Essence for Glamour.<br /> <br /> But, as of 2e, maybe ephemerals just stay the way they are- that'd certainly make the Goblin Markets more interesting. Imagine spirits selling fetishes, ghosts trying to buy memories, Goetia dealing with crystallized concepts, and angels maintaining the supply and demand of Goblin Fruit for some yet another weird Infrastructure. Or maybe the Hedge does not support Twilight, so all ephemerals freely Materialize automatically. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:19:48-08:00","id":815508,"title":"","content":"I think the general idea is that the Shadow doesn't &quot;overlap&quot; with the Hedge the way it does the physical world. Twilight is more a state of being than a place, but it still relies on there being an otherworld (or multiple otherworlds) underlying the physical reality inhabited by material and materialized beings. The Hedge is just the Hedge, and is beyond the boundaries of the Shadow and the Underworld just a much as it is beyond the boundaries of the physical world. It may, in fact, even be possible to physically reach the Underworld from the Hedge, or directly from Arcadia, based on the writeup of the Gravewright Kith.<br /> <br /> That being said, it may be worth noting that not all Goblin Markets are actually in the Hedge. Some are physical places, albeit well hidden ones, that non-fey beings like mortals and vampires can theoretically find and interact with. So there's still room for Goblin Markets featuring ephemeral beings, if you're interested in that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:10:03-08:00","id":815577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/815142-nwod-ghosts-in-the-hedge?p=815339#post815339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I also remember someone in this forum saying that spirits who 'go native' to the Hedge effectually become hobgoblins, gaining a corporeal body and swapping their Essence for Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same page:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits don\u2019t venture into the Hedge \u2014 the Hedge is a barrier between Earth and Faerie, and the spirit world has no dominion here. A spirit forced or tricked into the Hedge Materializes, and over time, Glamour can replace ephemera, making the spirit into a hobgoblin (indeed, some theorize that this is how the Hedge become \u201cpopulated\u201d in the first place). A spirit bound into a fetish is safe from this effect. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, as of 2e, maybe ephemerals just stay the way they are- that'd certainly make the Goblin Markets more interesting. </div> </div> </div>The metaphysics have literally never been &quot;ephemeral beings moved into the Hedge immediately become hobgoblins.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:56:38-08:00","id":815762,"title":"","content":"So this is what it all means effectively. In the &quot;Real world&quot; Twilight exists as a side realm that is part of the real world. You can cross it into the Hisil or the Underworld, if you have special powers. Like Werewolves. you can cross directly into the Hisil, or use an Avernian gate to cross directly into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Twilight itself does not exist in the Hedge, therefore you cannot use it to cross from the other realms into the hedge.<br /> <br /> Spirits can with luck, invite, or power; come from the Hisil into Twilight, and manifest in the real world. If they then cross into the hedge they shift to become Hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> Ghosts can with luck, invite, or power; come from the Underworld into Twilight, and manifest in the real world. If they then cross into the hedge they shift to become Hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3640,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","user":"gwiber","date":". 01-24-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:15:33-08:00","id":815771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gwiber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/815142-nwod-ghosts-in-the-hedge?p=815762#post815762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is what it all means effectively. In the &quot;Real world&quot; Twilight exists as a side realm that is part of the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in any game except Mummy. Something being &quot;in Twilight&quot; is like saying it's &quot;in solid form.&quot; A ghost in Twilight at a haunted mansion isn't in another dimension, it's in the geographic location of the mansion and made of stuff whose basic state is to be invisible and intangible to anything other than other ghosts and objects made of ghost-stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they then cross into the hedge they shift to become Hobgoblins. </div> </div> </div>They <i>can</i>, with long-term exposure, <i>eventually </i>become hobgoblins, in much the same way as animals left in the Hedge might survive the adaptation process to become hobgoblins and hedgebeasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:39:02-08:00","id":815861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/815142-nwod-ghosts-in-the-hedge?p=815339#post815339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I also remember someone in this forum saying that spirits who 'go native' to the Hedge effectually become hobgoblins, gaining a corporeal body and swapping their Essence for Glamour.<br /> <br /> But, as of 2e, maybe ephemerals just stay the way they are- that'd certainly make the Goblin Markets more interesting. Imagine spirits selling fetishes, ghosts trying to buy memories, Goetia dealing with crystallized concepts, and angels maintaining the supply and demand of Goblin Fruit for some yet another weird Infrastructure. Or maybe the Hedge does not support Twilight, so all ephemerals freely Materialize automatically. Who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually that adapting to the environment seems to still be going on- In Beast it talks about the unfettered who spend too much time in the various realms changing accordingly, it even mentioned that an unfettered who spends too much time in the underworld and the hsil will become geist-like. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}